Everyone wants a seat in the Family Office space right now. Not everyone is ready for what comes with it.

Family Offices have become one of the hottest corners of wealth management, and professionals are queuing up to get in. But what most people overlook is that moving from a large institution to a Family Office can sometimes feel like a change of world. At a large institution, you're surrounded by colleagues, committees, and process. In a Family Office, the team is a fraction of the size, decisions are often shaped by the family's values and ideology, and emotion is part of the equation. The skills that made someone a star at the institution don't automatically transfer.

In this clip, Mark Tepsich from UBS and I discuss what institutional professionals should know before making the jump, and what families should look for when hiring from that world.

